Fix cmake warning

We were getting a warning from cmake (building k4Reco):

```
  The package name passed to `find_package_handle_standard_args` (streamlog)
  does not match the name of the calling package (ILCUTIL).  This can lead to
  problems in calling code that expects `find_package` result variables
  (e.g., `_FOUND`) to follow a certain pattern.
```

Suppress this warning by adding the NAME_MISMATCHED option to
the FIND_PACKAGE_HANDLE_STANDARD_ARGS in streamlogConfig.cmake.
